# What the runtime fingerprint must NOT hash.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (2026-08-11). `app.json` sets runtimeVersion policy
# "fingerprint", so Expo hashes the project before it can answer the manifest
# request the dev-client makes on connect. That was taking 60 SECONDS per request —
# every time, uncached — so the dev-client timed out and "Enter URL manually" looked
# like it did nothing at all. A whole afternoon of the app not opening was this.
#
# The cost was build output, not source: ios/build alone is 1.3 GB of derived
# artefacts that cannot change what the app IS. Ignoring derived and vendored trees
# leaves the fingerprint measuring what it is meant to measure — the inputs that
# decide whether a published update is compatible with an installed binary.
#
# DO NOT add source, app config, or native project files here. Ignoring something the
# app's identity really depends on would let an incompatible OTA update match a build
# it should have been refused by, which is the one failure this policy exists to stop.
ios/build/
android/build/
android/app/build/
ios/Pods/
.expo/
**/*.xcuserdatad
**/DerivedData/
